diff --git a/CHANGELOG.en.md b/CHANGELOG.en.md
index 0c7ded4..2578d0d 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.en.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.en.md
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 
 ### Fixes
 
-- Telsiz DJ: the first YouTube track added while the tab was in the background (or the desktop window was minimized) never started on that device and started in the middle once the page came to the front. The card is now drawn on a hidden page too, and the track starts together with the other devices. The announcement in the text room did not show the track's name ("added a YouTube track"), and now it goes out with the name: the name is awaited for up to 8 seconds (if the page is hidden or closed in the meantime the announcement goes out at once without it), if it arrives later the announcement of the person who added it is edited with the name. People who keep the conversation open see that edit without the edited label: the label is only hidden for an edit that only adds the name to an announcement without a name, keeps its video, and is made within 10 minutes of sending the announcement (with one minute allowed for delay). In a conversation opened later and for every other edit (turning an ordinary message into an announcement, changing the video) the label is shown. A file added with "Play in DJ" was never announced, and now it is announced with its name in the text room where the file is. This announcement is a message without an attachment, and older versions show it as plain text instead of saying "this audio file". The last action line on the DJ card and the Notifications line also read the name from the queue, and they keep the last known name after the track ends, is skipped or is stopped. In windows narrower than 1280 pixels the player in the corner covered the voice buttons of the radio card.
+- Telsiz DJ: the first YouTube track added while the tab was in the background (or the desktop window was minimized) never started on that device and started in the middle once the page came to the front. The card is now drawn on a hidden page too, and the track starts together with the other devices. The announcement in the text room did not show the track's name ("added a YouTube track"), and now it goes out with the name: the name is awaited for up to 8 seconds (if the page is hidden or closed in the meantime the announcement goes out at once without it), if it arrives later the announcement of the person who added it is edited with the name. People who keep the conversation open see that edit without the edited label: the label is only hidden for an edit that only adds the name to an announcement without a name, keeps its video, and is made within 10 minutes of sending the announcement (with one minute allowed for delay). In a conversation opened later and for every other edit (turning an ordinary message into an announcement, changing the video) the label is shown. A file added with "Play in DJ" was never announced, and now it is announced with its name in the text room where the file is. This announcement is a message without an attachment, and older versions show it as plain text instead of saying "this audio file". Announcements do not count as @ mentions: an @everyone or @username in the name of the file or in the text of a `/play` command, which the announcement does not show, gives no notification, sound or mention badge, and an @ in the name of the file is not a mention in the text older versions show either. The last action line on the DJ card and the Notifications line also read the name from the queue, and they keep the last known name after the track ends, is skipped or is stopped. In windows narrower than 1280 pixels the player in the corner covered the voice buttons of the radio card.
 - In the Arcade and Turquoise and Copper themes the border of the camera indicator on the radio card ("Your camera is on, everyone in the room can see it") and of the notice shown when someone starts sharing their screen was not drawn at all. The muted Microphone and active Camera buttons of a direct message call, the chip and panel of your own share, the Stop Watching button, the Telsiz DJ error box and the verified safety number button were also drawn in the text color instead of their own border color. Both themes now have live and danger border colors, and the borders show with at least 3:1 contrast on every surface.
 
