diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
index 7c0232f..2cbdeef 100644
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ A single YouTube frame is used for the whole session in the voice room. When the
 
 Audio file tracks play in a single `<audio>` element for the lifetime of the engine, and only the source address changes when the track changes. The interface draws the card right away on the engine's track and state events. While the page is hidden (a background tab, a minimized window) the browser holds back animation frames, so drawing is done with a timer, and the YouTube player area is drawn at least 200x200 in the background too and the track starts together with the other devices. When the card is not visible, the player is moved to one of the four corners and can be minimized. The engine's local hold (a minimized player, a minimized window or a window hidden in the tray reported in the desktop app by `telsizDesktop.onWindowState`, Pause in the system's media controls) only stops the player on that device and does not change the shared state. When the hold is released, the player jumps to the shared position. The hold from Pause in the media controls is lifted when the person leaves the voice room. The bar of the player in the corner shows a hold the person can release (media controls, minimize), and while it is active the bar's button does not pause the room and only releases the hold. A YouTube track is not played while its player is not visible, and the minimize and window holds apply only to YouTube tracks.
 
-When a track is added, the client of the person adding it sends an encrypted announcement message to the text room. The `d` field in the plaintext of the message is `{ op: 'add', src: 'yt', vid, title }`, `{ op: 'add', src: 'file', title }` for an audio file attached to the same message (`/play` with an attachment), or `{ op: 'add', src: 'fileref', title }` for an audio file in another message added with "Play in DJ". `title` is optional, the receiver removes control and direction characters from it and shortens it to at most 120 code points, and older clients ignore the field. A `fileref` announcement has no attachment. Older clients that do not know this source ignore the `d` field and show the text of the message, so the text of that announcement is the full translated announcement. The name of a YouTube track may not be known when it is added, and the first device that loads its player writes the name into the DJ state. The person adding waits up to 8 seconds, if no name arrives or the page is hidden or closed in the meantime the announcement goes out without it, and once the name arrives the person adding edits their own message. The server only checks the author of an edit, cannot see the body and does not keep its earlier version. So the edited label is only hidden for an edit the client followed in the open conversation and compared with the earlier version: the earlier version is a DJ announcement without a name that was never edited, the new version only adds the name with the same source and video, and the edit is made within 10 minutes of sending the announcement (with one minute allowed for delay). An edit whose earlier version is not known (the conversation was opened later, the page was reloaded) and every other edit shows the label.
+When a track is added, the client of the person adding it sends an encrypted announcement message to the text room. The `d` field in the plaintext of the message is `{ op: 'add', src: 'yt', vid, title }`, `{ op: 'add', src: 'file', title }` for an audio file attached to the same message (`/play` with an attachment), or `{ op: 'add', src: 'fileref', title }` for an audio file in another message added with "Play in DJ". `title` is optional, the receiver removes control and direction characters from it and shortens it to at most 120 code points, and older clients ignore the field. A `fileref` announcement has no attachment. Older clients that do not know this source ignore the `d` field and show the text of the message, so the text of that announcement is the full translated announcement. A Telsiz DJ announcement does not count as an @ mention: the client draws the announcement instead of the text in the message, and the mention counter, notifications and the Mentions Me filter in search do not look at the text of the announcement. The name in the text of a `fileref` announcement is chosen by the person who uploaded the file, and older clients look for mentions in that text, so every @ sign in the name is written as a full width at sign (U+FF20) in the text. The name of a YouTube track may not be known when it is added, and the first device that loads its player writes the name into the DJ state. The person adding waits up to 8 seconds, if no name arrives or the page is hidden or closed in the meantime the announcement goes out without it, and once the name arrives the person adding edits their own message. The server only checks the author of an edit, cannot see the body and does not keep its earlier version. So the edited label is only hidden for an edit the client followed in the open conversation and compared with the earlier version: the earlier version is a DJ announcement without a name that was never edited, the new version only adds the name with the same source and video, and the edit is made within 10 minutes of sending the announcement (with one minute allowed for delay). An edit whose earlier version is not known (the conversation was opened later, the page was reloaded) and every other edit shows the label.
 
 If the server owner turns off Telsiz DJ, the server rejects DJ writes. If the YouTube source is turned off, the restriction is applied on the members' devices, since the server cannot see the encrypted state. When restricted mode (`music.restricted`) is on and someone with the DJ permission is in the room, the server rejects writes from people without the permission with `403 dj_restricted`. If nobody with the DJ permission is in the room, everyone can write, so end of track transitions (the clients' automatic writes) continue after the DJ leaves.
 
diff --git a/docs/MIMARI.md b/docs/MIMARI.md
index 446a502..d312a64 100644
